This is a dish with very distinct regional variations. In Osaka-style okonomiy[aki], all the component ingredients are mixed together in a bowl of batter, then spread out on the grill for cooking. The[ Hiroshima] version is more complicated and takes longer to prepare, as the[ chef] (not the customer) assembles distinct layers of toppings, vegetables, noodles, fried egg and[ panc]ake base into the final product.
