The question of growing inequality is particularly relevant because preferential policies have predicated Shenzhen[�]�s competitive advantage. The most famous of the quotations in this regard was Deng[ Xia]oping[�]�s decision to “allow a few to get rich first[�]�. More to the point, in Shenzhen wages for manual labor remain more or less what they were over 15 years ago, while white collar salaries continue to rise.[ Meanwhile], the price of housing has gone up even faster than white collar salaries creating a situation in which most young people are trying to figure out if they will be able to purchase a home.
