I’m lucky if I can get going without returning for one last thing, like replacing the house phone for my cell, realizing I[�]�m not wearing my contacts, trading stiff shoes for a more comfortable pair, one more trip to bathroom, another smear of sunblock. Once I[�]�m finally on my way, it[�]�s a slight uphill hike and a reverse easy j[aunt] down.
